                <pb facs="0798" n="674" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg674"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/1969: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Representative on Special Mission in Cuba</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Crowder</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-01-21T14:00:00-05:29"><hi rendition="#italic">January 21,
                                1921—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 11:10
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>8. Reports thus far received from courts indicate necessity of special elections
                    on a scale which will place the choice of President in doubt. In conference held
                    this morning President Menocal expressed same view.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crowder</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
